#name;Hank
Good evening, contessa. How are you?

#name;Imelda
(dismissive) Oh, Henry, dear, you know how much I dislike you calling me that.

#name;Hank
And YOU know how much I dislike you calling me Henry.

#name;Imelda
Well, fine. (Both chuckle.) It’s been too long, darling. And to answer your question, I’m absolutely dreadful.

#name;Hank
Don Pappardelle was known for his exports and exterminations, not for being a good husband. Trouble in paradise?  

#name;Imelda
You could say that.

#name;Hank
What’s the matter, doll?

#name;Imelda
... I found the other woman. Some poor, sweet twenty-something. When I heard, I nearly chucked my pocketbook into the river. 

**[You poor thing.] -> Surprised
**[Are we surprised?] ->Right


==Surprised==
#name;Hank
You poor thing.

#name;Imelda
Can’t be surprised,of course. But it hurts, all the same... I had a life before the Don, you know.

#name;Hank
Do I ever! I remember when every club promoter in the city would saw a leg off to hear you sing.

#name;Imelda
And now... look at me! I’m washed up! He’s gotta pay. Hank? Will you do me a favor? (A beat. The grisly implication of her request hangs in the air.)

**[I (don’t) like where this is going.]

#name;Hank
I dont like where this is going

#name;Imelda
(It doesn’t matter,) It’s seamless. With the Tagliatelle land grab, he’ll be swimming with the fishes by St Patrick’s either way. I’ll just be expediting the process. Besides, you won’t be implicated.

#name;Hank
And how is that?

#name;Imelda
Cassio.

#name;Hank
Pappardelle’s consigliere. 

***[Baloney]->Baloney
***[Bullshit]->Bull

